cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "genolint: a static linter for genomics command-line scripts"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Ahmed"
    given-names: "Maaz"
    affiliation: "Ziauddin University, Karachi, Pakistan"
abstract: "genolint is a static linter for bcftools, samtools, GATK, SnpEff and SnpSift commands in shell scripts and Snakemake files. Six rules detect silent, tool-specific errors such as an output type that does not match the file extension, bcftools concat without --allow-overlaps, region queries on an unindexed file, partial SnpSift consequence terms and mixed chr/bare contig names."
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-03
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Maazxbioinfo/genolint"
keywords:
  - genomics
  - static analysis
  - linting
  - bcftools
  - bioinformatics
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23111608
